# Fix: Duplicate Draft Issue

## Root Cause Analysis
The user reported that the AI creates duplicate drafts and loops ("The draft has been saved. Would you like to send it?") instead of actually sending the email when told "Looks good, send it."

Analysis of the traces reveals a compounding issue:
1. **Hallucinated Drafts:** When told to "Draft a reply", the AI often outputs the text "I have drafted a reply..." *without actually calling the `reply_to_email` tool*. It thinks it can draft emails by just writing them in the chat.
2. **Draft Amnesia:** Because the AI didn't use the tool in the first turn, when the user says "Looks good, send it" in the next turn, the AI realizes the draft isn't actually in Outlook. It then calls `reply_to_email` to genuinely create it. 
3. **Forced Confirmation Loop:** The `reply_to_email` and [create_draft](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#365-394) tools contain instructions forcing the AI to ask the user for permission *again* after drafting. So instead of sending it right away, the AI asks "Would you like to send it?" again, confusing the user and creating duplicate drafts if the cycle repeats.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [orchestrator.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py)
We need to strengthen the `SYSTEM_PROMPT` to explicitly stop the AI from hallucinating drafts and re-drafting existing ones:

1. **Forbid Plain-Text Drafting:** Add a strict rule: "NEVER write a draft in plain text. You MUST actually use the [create_draft](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#365-394) or `reply_to_email` tools to create it in Outlook before showing the user."
2. **Handle "Send It" Requests:** Add a strict rule: "If the user says 'send it', DO NOT call [create_draft](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#365-394) or `reply_to_email` again. You MUST call [get_drafts](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#248-307) to find the Draft ID, and then call [send_draft](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#435-456)."

### [MODIFY] [outlook_client.py](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py)
1. **Remove Forced Confirmation on Redundant Actions:** Modify the `note` returned by [create_draft](file:///C:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#365-394) and `reply_to_email` to say: *"If the user ALREADY told you to send it, call send_draft immediately. Otherwise, ask for approval."* This will prevent the AI from getting stuck in an infinite "Would you like me to send it?" loop when it generates a draft on-demand.

## Verification Plan
1. Send a request: "Reply to Lab 4 email saying 'Code received'". 
2. Verify the AI calls `reply_to_email` immediately instead of just generating text.
3. Say "Send it", and verify the AI calls [get_drafts](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#248-307) → [send_draft](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/tools/outlook_client.py#435-456) without duplicating the draft.
